  "verbalization": "Glycine appears to be indirectly linked to the Common Cold through a series of pharmacological pathways involving respiratory conditions. The evidence suggests that Glycine is associated with Rhinitis, a condition that is in turn linked to the Common Cold via different medications—Guaifenesin, Clofedanol, and Dextromethorphan. These medications are commonly used to treat respiratory symptoms, and their association with the Common Cold implies a potential role in symptom management or pathophysiology. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Glycine might influence respiratory health, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The evidence points to a network of interactions involving respiratory conditions and their treatment, but the direct causal link between Glycine and the Common Cold remains speculative.",
